:"Volsdalen Church (Norwegian: Volsdalen kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located on the south side of the island of Nørvøya in the town of Ålesund. It is one of the three churches for Ålesund and Volsdalen parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Volsdalen Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Alesund_-_Voldsdalen_kirke_-_Exterior_-_2.jpg/960px-Alesund_-_Voldsdalen_kirke_-_Exterior_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nørve","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.4753,"lo":6.2029,"d":2590,"ds":"Nørve (or Nørvøya) is an island in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is the largest of the islands containing the city center of Ålesund, the others being Aspøya and Hessa, located to the west. The 5-square-kilometre (1.9 sq mi) island of Nørve is located south of Ellingsøya, north of Sula, and west of Uksenøya.","wpu":"Nørve","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ed/Aksla_aalesund_MH5Y3793.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Ellingsøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.4936,"lo":6.1772,"d":2704,"ds":"Ellingsøya is an island in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. With an area of 22 square kilometres (8.5 sq mi), Ellingsøya is the second largest island in the municipality after Uksenøya. The island is located northeast of the town of Ålesund, north of the islands of Nørve and Uksenøya, east of the island of Valderøya, and south of the mainland peninsula of Haram Municipality.","wpu":"Ellingsøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ellings%C3%B8y.jpg/960px-Ellings%C3%B8y.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Atlantic Sea-Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.465556,"lo":6.095833,"d":3024,"ds":"The Atlantic Sea-Park (Norwegian: Atlanterhavsparken) is an aquarium in Ålesund, Norway. It was founded in 1951 as a limited company. The current facility was officially opened 15 June 1998.","wpu":"Atlantic Sea-Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Atlanterhavsparken-AlseundAquarium_P1080388.JPG/960px-Atlanterhavsparken-AlseundAquarium_P1080388.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Valderøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.4974,"lo":6.1189,"d":3323,"ds":"Valderøya is an island off the west coast of Norway. It is part of Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county. The 6.5-square-kilometre (2.5 sq mi) island had 4,153 residents in 2017.","wpu":"Valderøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Giske_kommune_-_Valderoya_4.jpg/960px-Giske_kommune_-_Valderoya_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Valderøy Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.503238,"lo":6.130263,"d":3664,"ds":"Valderøy Church (Norwegian: Valderøy kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located on the south side of the village of Nordstrand on the island of Valderøya. It is the church for the Valderøy parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Valderøy Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Valder%C3%B8y_kirke_fra_RA.jpg/960px-Valder%C3%B8y_kirke_fra_RA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Borgund Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.466301,"lo":6.233875,"d":4204,"ds":"Borgund Church (Norwegian: Borgund kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the village of Borgund, just east of the city of Ålesund. It is the church for the Borgund parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Borgund Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Borgund_kyrkje_i_Aalesund.jpg/960px-Borgund_kyrkje_i_Aalesund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sunnmøre Museum Foundation","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.468747,"lo":6.235967,"d":4279,"ds":"The Sunnmøre Museum Foundation (Norwegian: Stiftinga Sunnmøre Museum) is a foundation comprising 12 museums in the Sunnmøre traditional district of the western Norwegian county of Møre og Romsdal.","wpu":"Sunnmøre Museum Foundation","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/2004-05-28-YtsteSkotet11.JPG/960px-2004-05-28-YtsteSkotet11.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Langevåg Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.439599,"lo":6.204842,"d":4481,"ds":"Langevåg Church (Norwegian: Langevåg kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Sula Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the village of Langevåg on the northern shore of the island of Sula. It is one of the two churches for the Sula parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Langevåg Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Langev%C3%A5g_kirke_fra_RA.jpg/960px-Langev%C3%A5g_kirke_fra_RA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Godøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.476394,"lo":6.040381,"d":5807,"ds":"Godøya is an island in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The island is famous for its beautiful nature, dominated by the 497-metre (1,631 ft) tall mountain Storhornet and the large lake Alnesvatnet. The 10.9-square-kilometre (4.2 sq mi) island had 1,151 residents in 2019.","wpu":"Godøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Giske_kommune_-_Godoya_1.jpg/960px-Giske_kommune_-_Godoya_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Giske Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.498642,"lo":6.050228,"d":6053,"ds":"Giske Church (Norwegian: Giske kyrkje) is a 12th-century marble parish church of the Church of Norway in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located on the south side of the island of Giske, about 10 kilometres (6.2 mi) northwest of the town of Ålesund. It is the main church for the Giske parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Giske Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Giske_kyrkje.jpg/960px-Giske_kyrkje.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ellingsøy Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.49221,"lo":6.271546,"d":6491,"ds":"Ellingsøy Church (Norwegian: Ellingsøy kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located on the island of Ellingsøya, just west of the village of Myklebost. It is the church for the Ellingsøy parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Ellingsøy Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Ellings%C3%B8y_kirke_fra_KMB.jpg/960px-Ellings%C3%B8y_kirke_fra_KMB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Giske (island)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.5024,"lo":6.0396,"d":6734,"ds":"Giske is an island in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It covers an area of 2.67 square kilometers (1.03 sq mi). It is flat, with the highest point 23 meters (75 ft) above mean sea level.","wpu":"Giske (island)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Snowclad_Giske.jpg/960px-Snowclad_Giske.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Godøy Chapel","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.468321,"lo":6.01511,"d":7098,"ds":"Godøy Chapel (Norwegian: Godøy kapell) is a chapel of the Church of Norway in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located on the small island of Godøy. It is an annex chapel in the Giske parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Godøy Chapel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/God%C3%B8y_kirke.jpg/960px-God%C3%B8y_kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hamnsund Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.531963,"lo":6.26899,"d":8939,"ds":"Hamnsund Church (Norwegian: Hamnsund kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Haram Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the village of Søvik. It is the church for the Hamnsund parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Hamnsund Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Hamnsund_kirke_i_S%C3%B8vik.jpg/960px-Hamnsund_kirke_i_S%C3%B8vik.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Indre Sula Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.427401,"lo":6.299629,"d":9025,"ds":"Indre Sula Church (Norwegian: Indre Sula kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Sula Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the village of Mauseidvåg on the island of Sula. It is one of the two churches for the Sula parish which is part of the Nordre Sunnmøre prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Indre Sula Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Indre_Sula_kyrkje_-_6037_Eidsnes.jpeg/960px-Indre_Sula_kyrkje_-_6037_Eidsnes.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Alnes Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.489944,"lo":5.967222,"d":9751,"ds":"Alnes Lighthouse (Norwegian: Alnes fyrstasjon) was established in 1852 to guide fishing boats safely to the harbor of the small fishing community of Alnes on the north side of the island of Godøya in Giske Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The lighthouse sits about 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) northwest of Leitebakk.","wpu":"Alnes Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Alnesfyr.jpg/960px-Alnesfyr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ålesund (Norwegian pronunciation: [ˈôːɫəsʉn] ) is a town in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The town is the administrative centre of Ålesund Municipality. The centre of the town of Ålesund lies on the islands of Hessa, Aspøya, and Nørve with newer developments located on the islands of Uksenøya the outer parts of the \"urban area\" even stretch onto the island of Sula which is in the neighboring Sula Municipality.","wpu":"Ålesund","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/View_on_%C3%85lesund.jpg/960px-View_on_%C3%85lesund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}